        <p>the following propesals in draft. namely :—The prom o- tars of the Warrington and Kuutsford Light Railway are prepared to promote, construct, and equip Light Rail- ways and Tramways without and within tee Borough of Warrington with the consent of the Corporation. In Novemoter next they are intending to apply to the Light Railway Commissioners for an order to construct Light Railways between the boundary of the Borough of War- rington and Lymm and Knutsford along the main roads. They are prepared to amplify this application so as to include the construction ot such Tramway lines within the Borough as may be lir continuation of these Light Railways as far within the Borough as may be arranged with the Corporation. At a future date to be agved upon.they will be prepared to proceed with the promotion and construction of all other lines witbin the Borough, as may be required. The promoters will undertake to construct and equip these lines, and to work them for a limited period. At the expire/on of this period, the Corporation to have the option to purchase the lines within the B orough Boundary at a price to be agreed upon beforehand. The Corporation of Warrington to undertake on their part to transfer to the promotion company their provision&amp; Order for Tramways, if obtained, and to support the application for Light Railways both with evidence-and consent when before the Light Railway Commigsion-ra, and to join with the promwers in has*,ening the obtaining of the necessary powers as much as possible. The Corpora,tioa also to undertake not to grant to any company or syndicate similar privileges within a sped- Bed period, and to enter into a firm agreement that be- fore purchasing the lines within the B)rough. they, the Corporation will agree to reciprocate traffic with the Light Railway Company without the boundary,and give and accept mutual runninz powers with the Light Rail- way Company over lines which may be in connection. If the whole of the line; within and without the Borough Boundary were constructed by one company, it is sug- gested that the electrical energy for bo.:11 Tramways and Light Railways may be economically obtained from the new Warrington IVectric Power Station. These pro- posals are made quite in a preliminary way, and if your committee favour them gnerilly, Ishall he glad to meet the Committee and discuss them more fully at any time with two days' notice.</p>
        <p>I am, dear Sir, frAithrully yours, J. H. SCOFTER. It was rnolvrd " Tint, while the committee are voisl- log to give support to the construction of a light railway from the borough to Lymin and Knutsford, they cannot recommend the Council to entertain the proposal of the Company to construct tramways within the Borough." The MAYOR rnovel the con Firmation of the minutes. Alderman FRANCOMB seconded, and the motion was agreed to, after which the Council rose.</p>
