        <p>I.—The first coupon is free, and no competitor can send in more than one free coupon. Enclose Id. stamp ever for other coupon used. One Shilling Postal Order must be enilose 1. if all the coupons on above sheet are used. Any number of coupons can be sent in if paid for at the rate of One Shilling for each 20. 2.—Cross all Postal Orders and keep the numbers. 3.—No competitor can take more than one share of the £lO prize. IL—The coupons must be forwarded to the Examiner Ofiloe Warrington, the envelope to' hel endorsed Football Coupon." so as to be delivered by the first post on Thursday moping. If the envelope bears Wednesday's postmark, it will be received up to 5 p.m. on Thursday. Coupons delivered by hand must be received net later than 9 a.m. on Thursday. s.—Competitors demanding a scrutiny must enclose fee of Ten Shillings, give number of Postal Order (if any), and num— ber of coupons sent. In the event of the claim proving correct the fee will be returned. 6.—ln the event of two or more competitors tying, prize money will be divided. 7.—A1l attempts in this competition must be made on coupons cut from this paper. B.—When not less than 40 attempts are made, the coupons of unsuccessful competitors for the coupon prize will be carried forward and added to the number sent in in the next competition, so that s4oner or later the coupon prize must bl won by regular competitors. 9.—The results will appear in the first issue following the result of the matches.</p>
