      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-10-06_WidnesExaminer_art0072" n="art0072">
        <p>UNSOLICITED TESTIMONY.</p>
        <p>No. I.—Mr. Owen, Ty Maio Farm, Newborough, writes as follows :—" I can give the highest praise to the valuable remedy, Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. I had long auffered from ability and Weakness.and ree:ly thought I should rever recover. My medical men vcre privately of the same opinion. But when I commeneed taking this Precious Medieine,to my great surprise end joy, as well as that of my family, I rapidly improved, and now feel myself qeite another being ; an' le' all ever praise Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters as The licst Remedy for Debility and Weakness. No. 2.—Mr. Edwards, of Williamstown. writes as fol- lows :—" I can safely say that Gwilym Evane' Quinine Bitters have done wonders for me. After suffering for twelve months from Debility, and trying several doctors and different remedies without any benefit, I was ad- vised to try Gwilym Evans' Quinise Bitters, and the re- sult has been good." No. 3.—Mr. Brookes. 89, Kelshaw-stre2t, Liverpool, writes ne follows :—" I have suffered from ledi vistion and Liver Complaint for many years, but atter taking the Wonderful Melicine, Gwilym Evana' Quinine Bitters for only two months,l am happy to say it has given me great relief." No. 4.—Mr. Evans. 41, Henry-street, Birmingham, writes as follows :—"I have very great pleasure in bear- ing testimony to the benefit I have received from taking Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. lam never without a boale in the housetand it is invaluable to me. I suffered very much from Indigestion. Nervousness, and Debility, and often I had very severe pains in my head, so that to me it has proved quite a boon, as I can rely upon it to give me relief. I confidently recommend it to everyone I meet who suffers in the same way, and my recommen- dation his always proved a blessing," Ne s.—Mrs. Kirkham, 31, Dunstall-street, Wolver- hampton. writes as follows :—" I have suffered from Indgestion and pains in the need from three to four years, but after takine two bottles of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, I feel completely cured, and never felt better in my life" No. 6.—Mn. Williams, 11, Surrey-lane, Bettersea. writes as follows :—" I snail not fail to recommend Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters to all sufferers that come under my notice, as it is a Medicine that I have proved to be more excellent even than what you profess it to be. Th. World-renownei Preparation is sold in bottles 2s 9.1 and 4a 6 I each, everywhere,or the Proprietors will forward direct on receipt of stamps to the above value carriage free. The Sole Proprietors are the Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, ',tawny, South Wales. Beware of Imitations. This is most im- portant. When purchasing, always see the name, " Gwilym Evans " on Label, Stamp, and Bottle,without which none are genuine.</p>
