        <head>SWIMMING.</head>
        <p>SWIMMING.</p>
        <p>In conneetion with Flamilton•street school a very Soo" cessful swimming club has been conduoted during the past seasen. The boys, over a hundred in number,have visited the baths in Legh-street evory week, and have' been initiate I into the usetil art of swimming. order to further encourage the b)ys in this pursuit. several prizes were awarded, and the comp,.tition for these on Fridsy af,ernoon last, w,..s very teen, Sir 1)01 competed for thechampionship of the sesool and an fig. citing finish was witnested. Osborne Sinclair won the championship and silver medal ; J. Stansfieli the secotil prize, and W: Flarrop the third. On eecetsl waS the time that divided the first and second, lai he saolo divided second and third. T.,vo prizss wer,, offared for the neatest dive, the fir t bein,r gezured by J. Aihbrooks and the second by J. S7ansfi-ld.</p>
