      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-10-06_WidnesExaminer_art0126" n="art0126">
        <head>MR. PEARSON'S FORTHCOMING</head>
        <p>MR. PEARSON'S FORTHCOMING</p>
        <p>CONCERT.</p>
        <p>The programme of Mr. Pearson's cencert to be given in the Parr Hell on Wednesday the 25-.. h inst., presents two features, at least, of absorbing interest. One is the appearance at these concerts of the world-renowned Meister Glee Singers whose charming solos and concerted music have, during several recent seasons, gained for them the position of undoubted favourites with the Warrineton musical public. The celebrated quartet will sing some of their characteristic gems—the quaint glee, the richly-harmonieed version of familiar airs, and the humorous parody of our street-rausic,being all down fee exemplification. Individual members of the quartet will also sing songs of high intrinsio merit, and oppor- tunity will here be given of listening to Mr. Charles Chilley who has quite recently allied himself with the Meisters. The other event which may be counted upon to" draw" is the re-appearance in Warrington after * long absence of Mons. Hollmsn the gifted violencellist This famous virtuoso will, amongst other items of sur- passing interest, play by desire, the brilliant Fantasia on Bizet's " Carmen," the performance of which has earned for Mons. Hollman high rank both as an exponent of technique and as a collaborateur in the pro- duction of solo pieces for his favourite instrument. The concert party will include Madame Dews, a contralto locally well-known mid held in high esteem, and Madame Bertha Moore, a soprano whose successful Mut Is vouched for by several highly commendatory tributes from the musical quidnuncs. Mr, Edgar Hulland is also announced to play two classical pianoforte soles.</p>
      </div>
