        <p>LATEST NEWS. TRANSVAAL CRISIS. REPORTED INVASION OF NATAL LAING'S NEK SEIZED BY BOERS. From the war correspondent of the "Daily Telegraph," Newcastle, Wednesday (12.10 p.m.). I have come on here by train from Charlestown. Boers nightly occupy Laing's Nek. They hold the mountains to the south- west of Volksrust in considerable force. To-day the for- ward advance of the Boers began with a general move- ment of their artillery. I learn that Majuba Hill will be occupied to-morrow. I saw an armour protected engine and train yesterday on the line near Sandspruit, and also a number of armed Baffin accompanying the Boer commandces. General Joubert is quite confident of his ability to defend the hills against the British in any event.</p>
